Note on content (the MIT grant above covers the CODE)

* The historical documents quoted in data/*.json are taken from public-domain
  editions (all published before 1930) and this project claims no new rights in
  them. Per-source attribution and archive.org links are stored on every record.
* 271 records are modern English renderings made by this project (flagged in
  their context as "Translated for Chronicle") — those renderings are offered
  under the same MIT terms as the code.
* Hero artwork: Jacques-Louis David, Bonaparte Crossing the Alps (1800), public
  domain, via Wikimedia Commons; credited on the landing screen.

Confirm this licence choice with the project owner before publishing.
